{"title": "Jergal", "pageid": 21212, "url": "https://bg3.wiki/wiki/Jergal", "categories": ["Gods"], "html": "<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><aside class=\"portable-infobox noexcerpt searchaux pi-background pi-theme-default pi-layout-default pi-type-creature\"><h2 class=\"pi-item pi-item-spacing pi-title\" data-source=\"name\">Jergal</h2><div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"title\">\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">The Final Scribe<br>Lord of Bones<br>The Lord of the End of Everything</div>\n</div><div class=\"pi-media-collection\" data-source=\"image\">\n\t<ul class=\"pi-media-collection-tabs\">\n\t\t<li class=\"pi-tab-link pi-item-spacing current\" data-pi-tab=\"pi-tab-1\">Banner</li><li class=\"pi-tab-link pi-item-spacing\" data-pi-tab=\"pi-tab-2\">Symbol</li>\n\t</ul>\n\t\t<div class=\"pi-media-collection-tab-content current\" id=\"pi-tab-1\">\n\t\t\t<figure class=\"pi-item pi-media pi-image\" data-source=\"image\">\n\t\t\t\t<a href=\"/w/images/9/96/Jergal_Symbol.webp\" class=\"image image-thumbnail\" title=\"Banner\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<img src=\"/w/images/thumb/9/96/Jergal_Symbol.webp/300px-Jergal_Symbol.webp\" srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/9/96/Jergal_Symbol.webp/300px-Jergal_Symbol.webp 1x, /w/images/9/96/Jergal_Symbol.webp 2x\" class=\"pi-image-thumbnail\" alt=\"Banner\" width=\"270\" height=\"395\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t</figure>\n\t\t</div>\n\t\t<div class=\"pi-media-collection-tab-content\" id=\"pi-tab-2\">\n\t\t\t<figure class=\"pi-item pi-media pi-image\" data-source=\"image\">\n\t\t\t\t<a href=\"/w/images/9/9f/Jergal_Symbol2.webp\" class=\"image image-thumbnail\" title=\"Symbol\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<img src=\"/w/images/9/9f/Jergal_Symbol2.webp\" srcset=\"/w/images/9/9f/Jergal_Symbol2.webp 1x, /w/images/9/9f/Jergal_Symbol2.webp 2x\" class=\"pi-image-thumbnail\" alt=\"Symbol\" width=\"270\" height=\"352\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t</figure>\n\t\t</div>\n</div><section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\"><h2 class=\"pi-item pi-header pi-secondary-font pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-background\">Stats</h2><div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"race\">\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Race</h3>\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Deity\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Deity\">Deity</a></div>\n</div></section></aside>\n<b>Jergal</b>, also known as <i>The Final Scribe</i>, <i>Lord of Bones</i>,  <i>The Lord of the End of Everything</i> and many other names, was god of death for aeons until the rise of the <a href=\"/wiki/Dead_Three\" title=\"Dead Three\">Dead Three</a>.<sup id=\"cite_ref-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n\n<center class=\"noexcerpt\">\n<table style=\"background: none;\">\n\n<tbody><tr>\n<td rowspan=\"2\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><span><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/5/5b/Book_Generic_J_Unfaded.png/64px-Book_Generic_J_Unfaded.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/5/5b/Book_Generic_J_Unfaded.png/96px-Book_Generic_J_Unfaded.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/5/5b/Book_Generic_J_Unfaded.png/128px-Book_Generic_J_Unfaded.png.webp 2x\"><img src=\"/w/images/thumb/5/5b/Book_Generic_J_Unfaded.png/64px-Book_Generic_J_Unfaded.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></span><a href=\"/w/images/5/5b/Book_Generic_J_Unfaded.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span>\n</td>\n<td style=\"color: #C1A878; font-size: 3.3em; font-family: serif; font-weight: bold; padding: 4px 2px 2px; width: 0.5em; vertical-align: top;\">“\n</td>\n<td><blockquote style=\"margin: 0; font-style: italic\">Jergal, or so it's often said,\n<p>Once gave away his bony throne.\n</p><p>For Kelemvor he tracks the dead,\n</p>\nMakes sure that dead souls do not roam.</blockquote>\n</td>\n<td style=\"color: #C1A878; font-size: 3.3em; font-family: serif; font-weight: bold; padding: 4px 2px 2px; width: 0.5em; vertical-align: bottom;\">„\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\"><small>— <b><a href=\"/wiki/A_is_for_Azuth,_and_other_Gods_VI\" title=\"A is for Azuth, and other Gods VI\">A is for Azuth, and other Gods VI</a></b></small>\n</td>\n<td>\n</td></tr></tbody></table></center>\n<p><br>\n</p>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Overview\">Overview</span></h2>\n<p>Jergal is associated with the domains of <a href=\"/wiki/Knowledge_Domain\" title=\"Knowledge Domain\">Knowledge</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/Death_Domain\" title=\"Death Domain\">Death</a>. Jergal was the ancient god of death, till he gave up his powers and divided them among the <a href=\"/wiki/Dead_Three\" title=\"Dead Three\">Dead Three</a>. However, he still retains significant divine might, including physical invulnerability, the ability to portend fate, and resurrect and keep the dead.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Related_items\">Related items</span></h2>\n<ul><li><span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-block\" style=\"gap: 6px\"><span class=\"nowrap bg3wiki-icontext-icon\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-itemicon bg3wiki-itemicon-common\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Book_of_Dead_Gods\" title=\"Book of Dead Gods\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/0/0a/Book_Tome_E_Item_Icon.png/30px-Book_Tome_E_Item_Icon.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/0/0a/Book_Tome_E_Item_Icon.png/45px-Book_Tome_E_Item_Icon.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/0/0a/Book_Tome_E_Item_Icon.png/60px-Book_Tome_E_Item_Icon.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/0/0a/Book_Tome_E_Item_Icon.png/30px-Book_Tome_E_Item_Icon.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"30\" height=\"30\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/0/0a/Book_Tome_E_Item_Icon.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span></span><a href=\"/wiki/Book_of_Dead_Gods\" title=\"Book of Dead Gods\">Book of Dead Gods</a></span></li>\n<li><span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-block\" style=\"gap: 6px\"><span class=\"nowrap bg3wiki-icontext-icon\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-itemicon bg3wiki-itemicon-rare\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/The_Amulet_of_Lost_Voices\" title=\"The Amulet of Lost Voices\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/7/76/Amulet_of_Lost_Voices_Unfaded_Icon.png/30px-Amulet_of_Lost_Voices_Unfaded_Icon.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/7/76/Amulet_of_Lost_Voices_Unfaded_Icon.png/45px-Amulet_of_Lost_Voices_Unfaded_Icon.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/7/76/Amulet_of_Lost_Voices_Unfaded_Icon.png/60px-Amulet_of_Lost_Voices_Unfaded_Icon.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/7/76/Amulet_of_Lost_Voices_Unfaded_Icon.png/30px-Amulet_of_Lost_Voices_Unfaded_Icon.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"30\" height=\"30\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/7/76/Amulet_of_Lost_Voices_Unfaded_Icon.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span></span><a href=\"/wiki/The_Amulet_of_Lost_Voices\" title=\"The Amulet of Lost Voices\">The Amulet of Lost Voices</a></span></li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Related_literature\">Related literature</span></h2>\n<ul><li><span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-block\" style=\"gap: 6px\"><span class=\"nowrap bg3wiki-icontext-icon\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-itemicon bg3wiki-itemicon-common\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/A_is_for_Azuth,_and_other_Gods_VI\" title=\"A is for Azuth, and other Gods VI\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/d/d7/Book_Generic_J_Item_Icon.png/30px-Book_Generic_J_Item_Icon.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/d/d7/Book_Generic_J_Item_Icon.png/45px-Book_Generic_J_Item_Icon.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/d/d7/Book_Generic_J_Item_Icon.png/60px-Book_Generic_J_Item_Icon.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/d/d7/Book_Generic_J_Item_Icon.png/30px-Book_Generic_J_Item_Icon.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"30\" height=\"30\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/d/d7/Book_Generic_J_Item_Icon.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span></span><a href=\"/wiki/A_is_for_Azuth,_and_other_Gods_VI\" title=\"A is for Azuth, and other Gods VI\">A is for Azuth, and other Gods VI</a></span></li>\n<li><span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-block\" style=\"gap: 6px\"><span class=\"nowrap bg3wiki-icontext-icon\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-itemicon bg3wiki-itemicon-common\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Crumbling_Journal\" title=\"Crumbling Journal\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/a/ad/Book_Tome_J_Item_Icon.png/30px-Book_Tome_J_Item_Icon.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/a/ad/Book_Tome_J_Item_Icon.png/45px-Book_Tome_J_Item_Icon.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/a/ad/Book_Tome_J_Item_Icon.png/60px-Book_Tome_J_Item_Icon.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/a/ad/Book_Tome_J_Item_Icon.png/30px-Book_Tome_J_Item_Icon.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"30\" height=\"30\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/a/ad/Book_Tome_J_Item_Icon.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span></span><a href=\"/wiki/Crumbling_Journal\" title=\"Crumbling Journal\">Crumbling Journal</a></span></li>\n<li><span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-block\" style=\"gap: 6px\"><span class=\"nowrap bg3wiki-icontext-icon\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-itemicon bg3wiki-itemicon-common\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Death_%26_Divinity:_A_Godly_Guide\" title=\"Death &amp; Divinity: A Godly Guide\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/f/f3/Book_Tome_W_Item_Icon.png/30px-Book_Tome_W_Item_Icon.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/f/f3/Book_Tome_W_Item_Icon.png/45px-Book_Tome_W_Item_Icon.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/f/f3/Book_Tome_W_Item_Icon.png/60px-Book_Tome_W_Item_Icon.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/f/f3/Book_Tome_W_Item_Icon.png/30px-Book_Tome_W_Item_Icon.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"30\" height=\"30\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/f/f3/Book_Tome_W_Item_Icon.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span></span><a href=\"/wiki/Death_%26_Divinity:_A_Godly_Guide\" title=\"Death &amp; Divinity: A Godly Guide\">Death &amp; Divinity: A Godly Guide</a></span></li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Related_locations\">Related locations</span></h2>\n<ul><li><span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"mw-default-size bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Overgrown_Ruins#Dank_Crypt\" title=\"Overgrown Ruins\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/0/02/Custom_Map_Icon.png/25px-Custom_Map_Icon.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/0/02/Custom_Map_Icon.png/38px-Custom_Map_Icon.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/0/02/Custom_Map_Icon.png/50px-Custom_Map_Icon.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"Dank Crypt\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/0/02/Custom_Map_Icon.png/25px-Custom_Map_Icon.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"25\" height=\"25\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/0/02/Custom_Map_Icon.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span>⁠<a href=\"/wiki/Overgrown_Ruins#Dank_Crypt\" title=\"Overgrown Ruins\">Dank Crypt</a></li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Withers\">Withers</span></h2>\n<p>While the game never states it outright, it is heavily implied that <span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"mw-default-size bg3wiki-icon bg3wiki-round-image\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Withers\" title=\"Withers\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/2/25/Portrait_Withers.png/25px-Portrait_Withers.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/2/25/Portrait_Withers.png/38px-Portrait_Withers.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/2/25/Portrait_Withers.png/50px-Portrait_Withers.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"Withers\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/2/25/Portrait_Withers.png/25px-Portrait_Withers.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"25\" height=\"25\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/2/25/Portrait_Withers.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/Withers\" title=\"Withers\">Withers</a> is either an avatar of Jergal or Jergal himself. \n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"In-game_information\">In-game information</span></h3>\n<ul><li>He is found at the <a href=\"/wiki/Dank_Crypt\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Dank Crypt\">Shrine of Jergal</a>; a successful <a href=\"/wiki/Religion\" title=\"Religion\">Religion</a> check confirms that this is a shrine of Jergal and the undead scribes there bear Jergal's insignia.</li>\n<li>The <span class=\"nowrap bg3wiki-icontext-icon\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-itemicon bg3wiki-itemicon-common\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Book_of_Dead_Gods\" title=\"Book of Dead Gods\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/0/0a/Book_Tome_E_Item_Icon.png/20px-Book_Tome_E_Item_Icon.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/0/0a/Book_Tome_E_Item_Icon.png/30px-Book_Tome_E_Item_Icon.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/0/0a/Book_Tome_E_Item_Icon.png/40px-Book_Tome_E_Item_Icon.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/0/0a/Book_Tome_E_Item_Icon.png/20px-Book_Tome_E_Item_Icon.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/0/0a/Book_Tome_E_Item_Icon.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/Book_of_Dead_Gods\" title=\"Book of Dead Gods\">Book of Dead Gods</a> can be found nearby, containing a clear reference to the <a href=\"/wiki/Dead_Three\" title=\"Dead Three\">Dead Three</a>.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Paladin\" title=\"Paladin\">Paladins</a> or <a href=\"/wiki/Cleric\" title=\"Cleric\">Clerics</a> can feel divine energy from Withers. <i>\"He has a divine aspect, yes. A reflection of death itself. Eternal and inescapable.\"</i> If asking him if he is a god's Chosen, he refuses to answer.</li>\n<li>When first spoken to by a companion, Withers remarks <i>\"Ah, another. Thy name has been recorded.\"</i> alluding to his title as <i>\"the Final Scribe\"</i></li>\n<li>Likewise when a party member dies, as Withers resurrects them, he says <i>\"I strike thy name from the archives\"</i>.</li>\n<li>Clerics of <span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Kelemvor\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/6/68/FRWiki_Icon.png/22px-FRWiki_Icon.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/6/68/FRWiki_Icon.png/33px-FRWiki_Icon.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/6/68/FRWiki_Icon.png/44px-FRWiki_Icon.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"Kelemvor\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/6/68/FRWiki_Icon.png/22px-FRWiki_Icon.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"22\" height=\"22\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/6/68/FRWiki_Icon.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> <span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-extlink\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Kelemvor\">Kelemvor</a></span> have unique dialogue when talking to Withers and sense something familiar about him upon first meeting. He says unique lines such as, <i>\"Thou walk with death, child of Kelemvor. That is enough for an understanding between us\"</i> and, <i>\"No, although Kelemvor chose wise to bless one such as yourself\"</i> when replying to the player character's questions.</li>\n<li>When talking to Withers in <a href=\"/wiki/Moonrise_Towers\" title=\"Moonrise Towers\">Moonrise Towers</a>, the participant can note he seems to know a lot about the Dead Three.</li>\n<li>In the <a href=\"/wiki/Ancient_Mausoleum\" title=\"Ancient Mausoleum\">Ancient Mausoleum</a>, a <span class=\"nowrap bg3wiki-icontext-icon\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-itemicon bg3wiki-itemicon-common\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Crumbling_Journal\" title=\"Crumbling Journal\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/a/ad/Book_Tome_J_Item_Icon.png/20px-Book_Tome_J_Item_Icon.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/a/ad/Book_Tome_J_Item_Icon.png/30px-Book_Tome_J_Item_Icon.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/a/ad/Book_Tome_J_Item_Icon.png/40px-Book_Tome_J_Item_Icon.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/a/ad/Book_Tome_J_Item_Icon.png/20px-Book_Tome_J_Item_Icon.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/a/ad/Book_Tome_J_Item_Icon.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/Crumbling_Journal\" title=\"Crumbling Journal\">Crumbling Journal</a> can be found, detailing the encounter of a mortal with Jergal, with a description much alike Withers, which details his asking the same question that Withers does when the party first meet him: \"Masked in gold, his skin fine and worn as parchment. Jergal, the death-keeper, the End of Everything. I asked what he needed of me. He asked a simple question: “What is the worth of a single mortal's life?” \"</li>\n<li>At the <a href=\"/wiki/Epilogue\" title=\"Epilogue\">Epilogue</a> celebration player characters can find <span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"mw-default-size bg3wiki-icon bg3wiki-round-image\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Milil\" title=\"Milil\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/2/25/Portrait_Milil.png/25px-Portrait_Milil.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/2/25/Portrait_Milil.png/38px-Portrait_Milil.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/2/25/Portrait_Milil.png/50px-Portrait_Milil.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"Milil\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/2/25/Portrait_Milil.png/25px-Portrait_Milil.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"25\" height=\"25\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/2/25/Portrait_Milil.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/Milil\" title=\"Milil\">Milil</a>, a minor deity of song, poetry and inspiration, performing as entertainment. When spoken to, Milil explains that Withers saved him from being trapped in the <span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Fugue_Plane\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/6/68/FRWiki_Icon.png/22px-FRWiki_Icon.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/6/68/FRWiki_Icon.png/33px-FRWiki_Icon.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/6/68/FRWiki_Icon.png/44px-FRWiki_Icon.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"Fugue Plane\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/6/68/FRWiki_Icon.png/22px-FRWiki_Icon.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"22\" height=\"22\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/6/68/FRWiki_Icon.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> <span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-extlink\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Fugue_Plane\">Fugue Plane</a></span> by <span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Cyric\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/6/68/FRWiki_Icon.png/22px-FRWiki_Icon.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/6/68/FRWiki_Icon.png/33px-FRWiki_Icon.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/6/68/FRWiki_Icon.png/44px-FRWiki_Icon.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"Cyric\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/6/68/FRWiki_Icon.png/22px-FRWiki_Icon.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"22\" height=\"22\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/6/68/FRWiki_Icon.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> <span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-extlink\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Cyric\">Cyric</a></span>. He adds that he always performs at Withers' parties and is glad to do so, showing that Withers' powers affect even gods, all but confirming Withers is indeed Jergal.\n<ul><li>This is further shown if the player character attacks another one at the party. Withers approaches, reprimands them for it, opens a portal to the Fugue Plane and effortlessly hurls the player character into it, ending the playthrough. This happens to all player characters, even ones such as a Mind Flayer or <span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"mw-default-size bg3wiki-icon bg3wiki-round-image\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Gale\" title=\"Gale\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/1/11/Portrait_Gale.png/25px-Portrait_Gale.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/1/11/Portrait_Gale.png/38px-Portrait_Gale.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/1/11/Portrait_Gale.png/50px-Portrait_Gale.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"Gale\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/1/11/Portrait_Gale.png/25px-Portrait_Gale.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"25\" height=\"25\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/1/11/Portrait_Gale.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/Gale\" title=\"Gale\">Gale</a> if he became the God of Ambition.</li></ul></li>\n<li>In the post credits scene, Withers is seen talking to a mural of the Dead Three, expressing disappointment of their actions and telling them that he (regrettably) overestimated them. The way he speaks to the mural appears as that of someone who is familiar with the Three, which Jergal certainly would be.</li>\n<li>In the ending in which the Dark Urge is imprisoned after killing the <a href=\"/wiki/Netherbrain\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Netherbrain\">Netherbrain</a>, Withers visits the <a href=\"/wiki/Dark_Urge\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Dark Urge\">Dark Urge</a> in their cell. Driven mad by <a href=\"/wiki/Bhaal\" title=\"Bhaal\">Bhaal's</a> influence, the Dark Urge has the option to lash out at Withers and proclaim their desire to strip the skin from his \"god-meat\", further confirmation of Withers' divine nature.</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Datamined_and_other_content\">Datamined and other content</span></h3>\n<p>According to datamined notes, <span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"mw-default-size bg3wiki-icon bg3wiki-round-image\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Withers\" title=\"Withers\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/2/25/Portrait_Withers.png/25px-Portrait_Withers.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/2/25/Portrait_Withers.png/38px-Portrait_Withers.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/2/25/Portrait_Withers.png/50px-Portrait_Withers.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"Withers\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/2/25/Portrait_Withers.png/25px-Portrait_Withers.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"25\" height=\"25\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/2/25/Portrait_Withers.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/Withers\" title=\"Withers\">Withers</a> <i>is</i> Jergal. The datamined notes say he is compelled by <span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-icon bg3wiki-round-image\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Helm_(deity)\" title=\"Helm (deity)\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/b/b5/Helm_Icon.webp/11px-Helm_Icon.webp, /w/images/thumb/b/b5/Helm_Icon.webp/17px-Helm_Icon.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/b/b5/Helm_Icon.webp/22px-Helm_Icon.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"Helm\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/b/b5/Helm_Icon.webp/11px-Helm_Icon.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"11\" height=\"20\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/b/b5/Helm_Icon.webp\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/Helm_(deity)\" title=\"Helm (deity)\">Helm</a> to assist the party as penance.\n</p>\n<ul><li>From the Chapel dialog notes:</li></ul>\n<center class=\"noexcerpt\">\n<table style=\"background: none;\">\n\n\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"color: #C1A878; font-size: 3.3em; font-family: serif; font-weight: bold; padding: 4px 2px 2px; width: 0.5em; vertical-align: top;\">“\n</td>\n<td><blockquote style=\"margin: 0; font-style: italic\">After the party has slain a group of undead scholars, the judge of death--Jergal--climbs out of his sarcophagus to greet them. He has been locked inside for years by the god Helm to atone for his part in raising the Dead Three, wicked gods who are now plotting to conquer the realms. Jergal is emotionless and excessively formal, both resigned to his fate and that of others. He is here to assist the party because that is his divine oath, not out of any true desire to act. Players can attempt to goad or attack him, but to minimal effect, as he is functionally immortal. His only goal was to see their faces, so he can find them at camp later to offer further assistance.</blockquote>\n</td>\n<td style=\"color: #C1A878; font-size: 3.3em; font-family: serif; font-weight: bold; padding: 4px 2px 2px; width: 0.5em; vertical-align: bottom;\">„\n</td></tr></tbody></table></center>\n<ul><li>From the Camp dialog notes:</li></ul>\n<center class=\"noexcerpt\">\n<table style=\"background: none;\">\n\n\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"color: #C1A878; font-size: 3.3em; font-family: serif; font-weight: bold; padding: 4px 2px 2px; width: 0.5em; vertical-align: top;\">“\n</td>\n<td><blockquote style=\"margin: 0; font-style: italic\">Jergal, a god of the dead, awaits the player in camp. He is bound by the judgment of another god - Helm - to assist the players as penance for past crimes. He provides resurrection services to the players.</blockquote>\n</td>\n<td style=\"color: #C1A878; font-size: 3.3em; font-family: serif; font-weight: bold; padding: 4px 2px 2px; width: 0.5em; vertical-align: bottom;\">„\n</td></tr></tbody></table></center>\n<ul><li>His texture files are named <span class=\"bg3wiki-info-blob\">SKEL_HUM_M_&lt;...&gt;_Jergal</span>.</li>\n<li>His flags are named <span class=\"bg3wiki-info-blob\">Jergal_&lt;...&gt;</span> (e.g. <span class=\"bg3wiki-info-blob\">Jergal_AskedAboutCalling</span> is set if the player character asks Withers why it is easy for him to resurrect fallen companions).</li>\n<li>Three steps in the quest <span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Explore_the_Ruins\" title=\"Explore the Ruins\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/6/69/Quest_Map_Icon.png/22px-Quest_Map_Icon.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/6/69/Quest_Map_Icon.png/33px-Quest_Map_Icon.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/6/69/Quest_Map_Icon.png/44px-Quest_Map_Icon.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"Explore the Ruins\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/6/69/Quest_Map_Icon.png/22px-Quest_Map_Icon.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"22\" height=\"22\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/6/69/Quest_Map_Icon.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span>⁠<a href=\"/wiki/Explore_the_Ruins\" title=\"Explore the Ruins\">Explore the Ruins</a> are named <span class=\"bg3wiki-info-blob\">...Jergal</span>:\n<ul><li><span class=\"bg3wiki-info-blob\">ConfrontJergal</span>: <i>That strange figure found our camp. What does he want?</i></li>\n<li><span class=\"bg3wiki-info-blob\">JergalAtCamp</span>: <i>That strange figure somehow found our camp. He was probably the ruins' greatest secret, but there could still be some treasure down there.</i></li>\n<li><span class=\"bg3wiki-info-blob\">ConnectedSarcophagusJergal</span>: <i>The strange figure admitted he was the 'Guardian of Tombs' and that he'd been sealed within one of the ruins' sarcophagi. He was likely the ruins' greatest secret.</i></li></ul></li>\n<li>In Withers' official concept art (see gallery below) he is referred to as Jergal.</li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Quotes\">Quotes</span></h2>\n<center class=\"noexcerpt\">\n<table style=\"background: none;\">\n\n<tbody><tr>\n<td rowspan=\"2\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><span><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/9/90/Jergal_Statue_Head.png/64px-Jergal_Statue_Head.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/9/90/Jergal_Statue_Head.png/96px-Jergal_Statue_Head.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/9/90/Jergal_Statue_Head.png/128px-Jergal_Statue_Head.png.webp 2x\"><img src=\"/w/images/thumb/9/90/Jergal_Statue_Head.png/64px-Jergal_Statue_Head.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"64\" height=\"76\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></span><a href=\"/w/images/9/90/Jergal_Statue_Head.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span>\n</td>\n<td style=\"color: #C1A878; font-size: 3.3em; font-family: serif; font-weight: bold; padding: 4px 2px 2px; width: 0.5em; vertical-align: top;\">“\n</td>\n<td><blockquote style=\"margin: 0; font-style: italic\">Jergal? This must be ancient - no one worships the Final Scribe anymore.</blockquote>\n</td>\n<td style=\"color: #C1A878; font-size: 3.3em; font-family: serif; font-weight: bold; padding: 4px 2px 2px; width: 0.5em; vertical-align: bottom;\">„\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\"><small>— <b>Reacting to a statue in the <a href=\"/wiki/Dank_Crypt\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Dank Crypt\">Dank Crypt</a></b></small>\n</td>\n<td>\n</td></tr></tbody></table></center>\n<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r356266\">.mw-parser-output .bg3wiki-fancy-quote{display:grid;margin:10px 4px}.mw-parser-output .bg3wiki-fancy-quote-blockquote-left,.mw-parser-output .bg3wiki-fancy-quote-blockquote-right{padding:8px 16px;margin:auto}@media screen and (max-width:779px){.mw-parser-output .bg3wiki-fancy-quote-blockquote-left,.mw-parser-output .bg3wiki-fancy-quote-blockquote-right{margin-top:10px;padding:8px 2px;border-left:0!important;grid-row:2;grid-column:2}.mw-parser-output .bg3wiki-fancy-quote-image-right,.mw-parser-output .bg3wiki-fancy-quote-image-left{margin:auto;grid-row:1;grid-column:2}.mw-parser-output .bg3wiki-fancy-quote-author{grid-row:3;grid-column:2}.mw-parser-output .bg3wiki-fancy-quote{justify-content:center!important}}@media screen and (min-width:780px){.mw-parser-output .bg3wiki-fancy-quote-blockquote-left{margin-left:10px;border-left:2px solid #3d3d3d!important;grid-row:1;grid-column:2}.mw-parser-output .bg3wiki-fancy-quote-blockquote-right{margin-right:10px;border-left:0!important;border-right:2px solid #3d3d3d;grid-row:1;grid-column:2}.mw-parser-output .bg3wiki-fancy-quote-image-right{margin:auto 0;grid-row:1;grid-column:3}.mw-parser-output .bg3wiki-fancy-quote-image-left{margin:auto 0;grid-row:1;grid-column:1}.mw-parser-output .bg3wiki-fancy-quote-author{grid-row:2;grid-column:2}}.mw-parser-output .bg3wiki-fancy-quote-author{margin-left:auto;margin-right:32px;font-size:smaller;font-weight:bold}.mw-parser-output .bg3wiki-fancy-quote-begin,.mw-parser-output .bg3wiki-fancy-quote-end{font-size:300%;font-family:serif;color:#3d3d3d;line-height:1em}.mw-parser-output .bg3wiki-fancy-quote-begin{margin-bottom:auto;margin-right:8px}.mw-parser-output .bg3wiki-fancy-quote-end{margin-top:auto;margin-left:8px}.mw-parser-output .bg3wiki-fancy-quote-text{font-style:italic}</style><div class=\"bg3wiki-fancy-quote\" style=\"justify-content: center\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-fancy-quote-image-left\" style=\"display: inline-block; height: calc(70px + 2*4px); width: calc(70px + 2*4px); clip-path: polygon(50% 0%, 100% 50%, 50% 100%, 0% 50%); background: black;\"><span style=\"display: inline-block; margin: 4px; width: 70px; height: 70px; clip-path: polygon(50% 0%, 100% 50%, 50% 100%, 0% 50%);\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Withers\" title=\"Withers\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/2/25/Portrait_Withers.png/70px-Portrait_Withers.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/2/25/Portrait_Withers.png/105px-Portrait_Withers.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/2/25/Portrait_Withers.png/140px-Portrait_Withers.png.webp 2x\"><img src=\"/w/images/thumb/2/25/Portrait_Withers.png/70px-Portrait_Withers.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"70\" height=\"70\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/2/25/Portrait_Withers.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span></span><blockquote style=\"font-size: 100%\" class=\"bg3wiki-fancy-quote-blockquote-left\">\n  <div style=\"display: flex; align-items: center\">\n     <div class=\"bg3wiki-fancy-quote-begin\">“</div>\n     <div class=\"bg3wiki-fancy-quote-text\">Once judged, ascended, then vanquished as one and as three.</div>\n     <div class=\"bg3wiki-fancy-quote-end\">„</div>\n  </div>\n</blockquote><div class=\"bg3wiki-fancy-quote-author\">— <a href=\"/wiki/Withers\" title=\"Withers\">Withers</a></div><div style=\"grid-column:3\"></div></div>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Gallery\">Gallery</span></h2>\n<ul class=\"gallery mw-gallery-packed\">\n\t\t<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 409.33333333333px\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 407.33333333333px;\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:Jane-katsubo-jergal-char.jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\" title=\"Official concept art by Jane Katsubo.\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/3/3e/Jane-katsubo-jergal-char.jpg/611px-Jane-katsubo-jergal-char.jpg.webp, /w/images/thumb/3/3e/Jane-katsubo-jergal-char.jpg/917px-Jane-katsubo-jergal-char.jpg.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/3/3e/Jane-katsubo-jergal-char.jpg/1222px-Jane-katsubo-jergal-char.jpg.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"Official concept art by Jane Katsubo.\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/3/3e/Jane-katsubo-jergal-char.jpg/611px-Jane-katsubo-jergal-char.jpg.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"408\" height=\"250\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/3/3e/Jane-katsubo-jergal-char.jpg\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></div>\n\t\t\t<div class=\"gallerytext\">Official concept art by Jane Katsubo.</div>\n\t\t</li>\n\t\t<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 166px\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 164px;\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:Withers_Jergal_Concept.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\" title=\"Concept art from the Digital Artbook.\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/2/21/Withers_Jergal_Concept.png/246px-Withers_Jergal_Concept.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/2/21/Withers_Jergal_Concept.png/369px-Withers_Jergal_Concept.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/2/21/Withers_Jergal_Concept.png/491px-Withers_Jergal_Concept.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"Concept art from the Digital Artbook.\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/2/21/Withers_Jergal_Concept.png/246px-Withers_Jergal_Concept.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"164\" height=\"250\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/2/21/Withers_Jergal_Concept.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></div>\n\t\t\t<div class=\"gallerytext\">Concept art from the Digital Artbook.</div>\n\t\t</li>\n\t\t<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 238px\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 236px;\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:Jergal_Concept_Art_Statue.webp\" class=\"mw-file-description\" title=\"Concept art of Jergal's statue.\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/c/ca/Jergal_Concept_Art_Statue.webp/354px-Jergal_Concept_Art_Statue.webp, /w/images/thumb/c/ca/Jergal_Concept_Art_Statue.webp/532px-Jergal_Concept_Art_Statue.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/c/ca/Jergal_Concept_Art_Statue.webp/708px-Jergal_Concept_Art_Statue.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"Concept art of Jergal's statue.\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/c/ca/Jergal_Concept_Art_Statue.webp/354px-Jergal_Concept_Art_Statue.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"236\" height=\"250\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/c/ca/Jergal_Concept_Art_Statue.webp\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></div>\n\t\t\t<div class=\"gallerytext\">Concept art of Jergal's statue.</div>\n\t\t</li>\n\t\t<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 434.66666666667px\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 432.66666666667px;\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:Jergal_Concept_Art_Statue_Set.webp\" class=\"mw-file-description\" title=\"Concept art of Jergal's statue.\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/8/8b/Jergal_Concept_Art_Statue_Set.webp/649px-Jergal_Concept_Art_Statue_Set.webp, /w/images/thumb/8/8b/Jergal_Concept_Art_Statue_Set.webp/974px-Jergal_Concept_Art_Statue_Set.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/8/8b/Jergal_Concept_Art_Statue_Set.webp/1298px-Jergal_Concept_Art_Statue_Set.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"Concept art of Jergal's statue.\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/8/8b/Jergal_Concept_Art_Statue_Set.webp/649px-Jergal_Concept_Art_Statue_Set.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"433\" height=\"250\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/8/8b/Jergal_Concept_Art_Statue_Set.webp\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></div>\n\t\t\t<div class=\"gallerytext\">Concept art of Jergal's statue.</div>\n\t\t</li>\n\t\t<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 378.66666666667px\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"thumb